SteamHead photographs and video — terms of reuse
================================================

Every photograph and every video frame on this site that shows an identifiable
person is © SteamHead, all rights reserved. It is NOT covered by the CC BY-SA
4.0 license in LICENSE-DOCS.

To reuse one, write to james@steamhead.space and say what you'd like to use and
what for.

Please do ask. SteamHead's whole purpose is spreading maker education, and
permission is granted readily for educational and non-commercial use. This is a
checkpoint, not a barrier, and the answer is usually yes.


Why these are reserved when everything else is open
---------------------------------------------------

A Creative Commons license grants copyright permissions and nothing else. It
does not — and cannot — grant the rights of the people in the photograph. Their
likeness and privacy rights are not SteamHead's to give away, and CC's own 4.0
text says as much.

Putting CC BY-SA on a photograph of a student would therefore promise something
SteamHead is not able to deliver. A reuser would reasonably read it as "I may
use this freely" when they would still need the consent of the person pictured,
with no way to obtain it.

Many of these photographs are of children. SteamHead holds media releases for
the MakeFashion Edu students and for the school events filmed for the YouTube
channel, and those releases do allow SteamHead to grant others permission in
turn — which is exactly why asking works here. The reservation stays anyway,
because a public license is irrevocable and cannot be conditioned on use, while
a permission granted on request can be scoped, and can be declined when a use
would not be right for the young person in the frame. Keeping that checkpoint is
the point of holding a release in the first place.


What counts
-----------

The line is "a photograph of a person", not "a photograph of a child". A reuser
cannot reliably tell a seventeen-year-old from a nineteen-year-old and should
not have to guess, and the adults in these photographs hold likeness rights too.

Photographs with no identifiable person in them — a close-up of a circuit, a
garment on a stand, an empty workshop — are ordinary documentation and fall
under CC BY-SA 4.0 with the rest of the site.


Photographer credits
--------------------

Some photographs carry a photographer's name in the filename or the caption.
SteamHead owns these images outright; the credits are there to send some signal
back to the photographers who shot them. If you're granted permission to reuse a
credited photograph, please carry the credit across.


Takedown
--------

If you appear in a photograph on this site, or you're the parent or guardian of
someone who does, and you'd like it removed, write to james@steamhead.space and
it will be taken down. You do not need to give a reason.
